  "id": "Compound::DB06637 - Gene::3748",
  "verbalization": "Dalfampridine is shown to interact with multiple potassium channel subunits through binding, with the specific targets Kcna6, Kcnf1, and Kcnv2 all participating in the same pathway involving Delayed Rectifier Potassium Channel Activity. This activity is ultimately linked to Kcnc3, suggesting a shared role in potassium channel regulation. The evidence indicates that Dalfampridine may influence Kcnc3 through a common mechanism involving delayed rectifier potassium channels, possibly by modulating their activity or expression. The high scores in all three paths suggest a consistent relationship, though the exact mechanism by which Dalfampridine affects Kcnc3 remains to be fully elucidated. The overlapping involvement of these channels in the same biological process supports a potential role for Dalfampridine in modulating potassium channel function, potentially through a shared regulatory pathway.",
